{"chunk_id": "00e6dc21764a", "text": "Sanjaya narrates Arjuna\u2019s reaction after witnessing Krishna\u2019s overwhelming universal form. Trembling and filled with awe and fear, Arjuna praises Krishna as the supreme reality\u2014greater than Brahman, the origin and essence of all gods and cosmic forces. Realizing he had previously addressed Krishna casually as a friend, Arjuna apologizes and begs forgiveness, acknowledging Krishna as the father and master of the universe. Overwhelmed by the terrifying vision, he asks Krishna to return to a gentler, familiar form. Krishna agrees, explaining that this universal form is exceedingly rare and cannot be seen through Vedic study, sacrifices, or austerities alone. True devotion is the path to knowing and attaining him. The chapter transitions into teachings on devotion (Bhakti), where Krishna describes the qualities and practices of those who reach him through steadfast, selfless devotion.\nArjuna praises Krishna\u2019s cosmic form, asks forgiveness and to see his gentle form again; Krishna teaches that devoted, selfless love is the sure path to reach him.\nThemes: divine revelation, devotion (bhakti), awe and fear of the divine, forgiveness and humility, paths to God", "vector": [0.01676894538104534, -0.008648758754134178, -0.010300545953214169, 0.0001866519742179662, 0.003242458449676633, 0.010439296253025532, -0.01291697658598423, -0.015658942982554436, -0.024591809138655663, 0.0016930820420384407, 0.000911786628421396, 0.015341800637543201, -0.02183002047240734, -0.006531167309731245, -0.014945372007787228, -0.002238171873614192, 0.04926290363073349, -0.022715378552675247, 0.014139299280941486, -0.0069969710893929005, -0.005589648149907589, -0.0017079480458050966, -0.014654656872153282, -0.012520547956228256, -0.009349116124212742, 0.01823573186993599, 0.0065840245224535465, -0.04054147005081177, 0.011919297277927399, -0.009639831259846687, -0.004535808227956295, 0.008675186894834042, 0.007386792916804552, -0.000802768